      "fit": 0.55
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "Driven by seasonal climate change, apprehended individuals have increased their attempts, their numbers a statistical trend that speaks of longing. While the border security effect maintains a low crossing numbers baseline, the true cost is the political deadlock on funding. Those who hold the power to unite or divide remain in a government impasse, their indecision a cold, public exposure that fails to address the deep human desire for connection that fuels this cycle of approach and apprehension.",
